| !Run for !CivServer - the Freeciv server in a TaskWindow.
| Start this first, then !Freeciv, and choose "Start new game": the client
| plays on this server. Type server commands (e.g. help, list, save) in the
| TaskWindow. The server program and the game's data are in !Freeciv, which
| must have been seen by the Filer (open the directory it's in).

IconSprites <Obey$Dir>.!Sprites
If "<Freeciv$Dir>"="" Then Error Open the directory with !Freeciv in it first: the server program and the game data are in !Freeciv.
Set Freeciv$Path <Freeciv$Dir>.
Obey <Freeciv$Dir>.Setup

| The server's output goes to its TaskWindow.
Unset FreecivServer$Output

| The window stays open when the server stops, so its last messages can be
| read; close it to finish. WimpSlot: the program with its tables is about
| 28MB; its heap is a dynamic area ("Freeciv server heap").
TaskWindow "Obey Freeciv:RunServer %*0" -wimpslot 36000K -name "Freeciv server" -display
